{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1021065-chiropteran-spies-examples-for-the-other-tribes","id":1021065,"title":"Chiropteran Spies - examples for the other tribes","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-22T16:22:35-08:00","id":1021065,"title":"Chiropteran Spies - examples for the other tribes","content":"The Chiropteran Spies talen is a figurine that can be animated for 12 hours. It is usually used as a scout or spy. The description says that Shadow Lords use wooden bats (hence the name), but that other tribes typically use some other form. Children of Gaia use porcelain doves, Glass Walkers use metal insects, and Silent Striders use clay scarabs. After being used, the figurine turns into a ruined pile of its base material (like sawdust).<br /> <br /> I'd like to come up with a list of default or standard forms used for the other tribes. Ideally, all of them should be an animal appropriate to the tribe, and some form of Craft involved to fashion an appropriate vessel made out of.<ul><li>For the Bone Gnawers I imagine some kind of chicken wire frame paper mache pigeon.</li> <li>Fianna use some kind of corn-doll (straw) shaped as a rabbit.</li> <li>Get of Fenris use a raven carved from pine wood.</li> <li>Red Talons are hard because I don't see them using human craftsmanship. They wouldn't want to work with human hands, a common problem for the tribe in creating any fetish or talen. However, I can see them organizing by paw and snout some kind of pile of feathers, leaves, or pinecones in some kind of artistic fashion that could become animated and blow along the wind or roll/crawl on the ground to accomplish the same.</li> <li>Silver Fangs probably use some kind of small bird of prey, like a kestrel fashioned by a silver metalworker. Silver would be most appropriate for the tribe in terms of looks, but at the same time it would be a difficult metal to use.</li> <li>I think Stargazers would use a superbly made origami butterfly from high quality paper.</li> <li>Uktena and Wendigo are hard for me as I want to only use animal species native to North America. Snakes would make the most sense for Uktena, but I think their capacity to be a useful scout or spy is limited. The Northern Cardinal has a range that closely mirrors what should be their protectorates, but I don't know what would be a good material for it. I think some kind of ice carving would be great for Wendigo, but can't think of a good animal - maybe a canada goose?</li> <li>I'm stuck on the Black Furies though. Maybe some kind of marine bird like a seagull.</li> </ul><br /> So what would be your suggestions? Have you see any unique depictions used by your fellow players or STs in your games?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T16:56:02-08:00","id":1021070,"title":"","content":"I like the idea of the Red Talons unearthing fossils and ritually imbuing them with Griffin's memory of the dead to temporarily bring back extinct creatures to act as spies. Passenger Pigeons, Ivory Billed Woodpeckers, \u0336Ma\u0336s\u0336t\u0336o\u0336d\u0336o\u0336n\u0336s\u0336, \u0336 they'd all make for great stealthy informants before vanishing into stone dust.<br /> <br /> I know fossils of recently dead species are pretty darn rare (I think there is only one partial fossil of a passenger pigeon wing, for example). It could always be handwaved as the Talons being guided to special hidden deposits of such things by Griffin's servants. I would rather the Talons imbue something rare, unspoiled and special and use their connections to the spirit world to create the talen, rather than have them craft something by hand or claw.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","user":"The Laughing Stranger","date":". 12-22-2016, 08:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T17:10:39-08:00","id":1021078,"title":"","content":"<br /> <br /> good ideas all<br /> <br /> Does it say explicitly that your telepathicly connected to a chiptorean spy?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T18:02:59-08:00","id":1021092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1021065-chiropteran-spies-examples-for-the-other-tribes?p=1021070#post1021070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the idea of the Red Talons unearthing fossils and ritually imbuing them with Griffin's memory of the dead to temporarily bring back extinct creatures to act as spies.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like! Instead of fossils of extinct animals, it could just be bones of prey animals slain be predators. Griffin is still a totem of hunting/predation so otherwise everything works and much easier to find bones of slain animals - Red Talons might even have to slay the animal itself!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1021065-chiropteran-spies-examples-for-the-other-tribes?p=1021078#post1021078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does it say explicitly that your telepathicly connected to a chiptorean spy?</div> </div> </div> </div>It is in the corebook write up so you can look up details yourself. There is no mention of any kind of communication at all, just that the figurines come to life. I imagine any communication would be appropriate animal sounds that the Talen activator understands, and likewise any commands to it just normal spoken words. I personally wouldn't allow any telepathic communication.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T22:59:18-08:00","id":1021167,"title":"","content":"Magpies for the Wendigo. They stick around even in winter, are highly intelligent, and have a fairly wide range. Several native tribes also view the magpie as either a gossip, a carrier of warnings, or just a straight up messenger.<br /> <br /> As for the Furies I can easily see them using something based off of an owl. Hecate was an Ancient Greek goddess who was known to transform into an owl and was also an aspect of the Crone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":3198,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3198-lunar-falcon","user":"Lunar Falcon","date":". 12-23-2016, 02:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3198-lunar-falcon","name":"Lunar Falcon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3198_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-23T13:36:15-08:00","id":1021385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lunar Falcon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1021065-chiropteran-spies-examples-for-the-other-tribes?p=1021167#post1021167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Magpies for the Wendigo. They stick around even in winter, are highly intelligent, and have a fairly wide range. Several native tribes also view the magpie as either a gossip, a carrier of warnings, or just a straight up messenger.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice pick. I think the black billed magpie would be an excellent choice for the Wendigo in the west, but after looking at its distribution map, its range doesn't cover the eastern Wendigo. I either need to find a counter part for those living in the east or some other animal that covers most of the territory. If it wasn't for its limited range, I think this would be a perfect choice!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lunar Falcon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1021065-chiropteran-spies-examples-for-the-other-tribes?p=1021167#post1021167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the Furies I can easily see them using something based off of an owl. Hecate was an Ancient Greek goddess who was known to transform into an owl and was also an aspect of the Crone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Owls would be appropriate in many respects, but I ended up not using them because Owl as a spirit is associated with the Silent Strider tribe. It is surprising that the description used a clay scarab instead of a small owl for the tribe, just like Shadow Lords used a bat instead of a crow. Maybe there is some kind of taboo/prohibition that you can't use the tribal totem? My preference is something that fits better with Pegasus' brood, but Axis Mundi does not give me many options or directions here. It is easy to find many animals that could be associated with the Furies, but not those that would make useful spies - relatively small, preferably with flight.<br /> <br /> Please share if you have any more ideas! These are good, and even if they are not perfect for me, others may like them.<br /> <br /> I don't think Garou talen makers would be limited to make these figurine spies only of the &quot;default&quot; creature and thus could do anything, but I would like a default of the most common animal for each tribe.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-23T14:02:29-08:00","id":1021396,"title":"","content":"oh with Talens and fetishes in general, how implausible is it for a garou to gain a few talens of other tribal construction as rewards for various missions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-23T16:19:44-08:00","id":1021427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1021065-chiropteran-spies-examples-for-the-other-tribes?p=1021396#post1021396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">oh with Talens and fetishes in general, how implausible is it for a garou to gain a few talens of other tribal construction as rewards for various missions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Talens are viewed more as tools and less like cherished heirlooms; giving a talen away as a token of trust or thanks makes a lot of sense. Heck, a Garou might even give away a fetish if a quest merits such a glorious reward, but that is pretty rare and exceptional.<br /> <br /> Just don't treat spirit-imbued items like door prizes and you will be fine!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-23T17:33:01-08:00","id":1021443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1021065-chiropteran-spies-examples-for-the-other-tribes?p=1021385#post1021385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nice pick. I think the black billed magpie would be an excellent choice for the Wendigo in the west, but after looking at its distribution map, its range doesn't cover the eastern Wendigo. I either need to find a counter part for those living in the east or some other animal that covers most of the territory. If it wasn't for its limited range, I think this would be a perfect choice!</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing with the Wendigo is that they count many different cultures as their Kinfolk so it makes perfect sense for them to have regional differences based off of their associated tribes. I am not sure how feasible it would be but the range of the extinct Passenger Pigeon is a pretty good eastern counterpart to the magpie. The species held great significance to North Eastern tribes with the Seneca even having a pigeon dance. I feel that the fact that the Europeans the Wendigo have such animosity towards having been the cause of the bird's extinction is another thing to promote that particular bird. The logistics of using an extinct animal spirit may not be something that is doable, however.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3198-lunar-falcon","name":"Lunar Falcon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3198_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}